# The loop ends within the array and an allocation always comes back, so the loop does not poll: the allocation is where a collection can start.
# The array may be old and every object is new, so each turn has the barrier of the array in line. The new object itself is filled without one.
# An allocation gives no array other storage, so the storage and its length are loaded ahead of the loop. The index is checked against that length.
# CHECK-LABEL: steps by 1
# CHECK-NOT: Patchpoint(
# CHECK: Int64 b@[[entry]] = Patchpoint({{*}}Writes:{collectorState, {{*}}:NewObject)
# CHECK-NEXT: Store(b@{{*}}, b@[[entry]], offset = 16, ControlDependent|Writes:ObjectFields{{*}}:NewObject)
# CHECK-NOT: Patchpoint(
# CHECK-NOT: Reads:JSArray_butterfly
# CHECK-NOT: Reads:Butterfly_publicLength
# CHECK: Store(b@[[entry]], b@{{*}}, ControlDependent|Writes:indexedContiguousProperties, {{*}}:PutArrayElement)
# CHECK-NEXT: Int32 b@[[threshold]] = Load(b@{{*}}, offset = {{*}}, ControlDependent|Reads:collectorState, {{*}}:PutArrayElement)
# CHECK-NEXT: Int32 b@[[state]] = Load8Z(b@{{*}}, offset = 7, ControlDependent|Reads:collectorState, {{*}}:PutArrayElement)
# CHECK-NEXT: Int32 b@[[isUnmarked]] = Below(b@[[threshold]], b@[[state]], {{*}}:PutArrayElement)
# CHECK-NEXT: Branch(b@[[isUnmarked]], Terminal, {{*}}:PutArrayElement)
# CHECK-NEXT: Successors: Then:#[[next]], Else:Rare:#
# CHECK-NEXT: BB#[[next]]:
# CHECK: Branch(b@{{*}}, Terminal, {{*}}:Less)
# CHECK-LABEL: end of loop
# A turn allocates, and the way round the allocator comes back into the loop: the loop polls on every turn. On ARM64 the rare way round the barrier has a copy of the poll.
# POLLS-LABEL: steps by 1
# POLLS-COUNT-1: isLoopPoll
# POLLS-NOT: isLoopPoll
# POLLS-LABEL: end of loop
# X64: loop #{{*}}, instructions: 13, patchpoints: 2
# ARM64: loop #{{*}}, instructions: 13, patchpoints: 2
